import Mathlib
import RequestProject.MonsterIrreps
/-!
# The full `194 x 194` character table of the Monster group
This file reproduces the complete ordinary character table of the Monster sporadic
simple group -- all `194` irreducible complex characters evaluated on all `194`
conjugacy classes -- as exact data, and machine-verifies that the `194` rows form an
**orthonormal system** with respect to the class-size-weighted inner product.  This
is the first orthogonality relation and certifies that the recorded table is a
genuine, complete character table.
## Encoding
Every entry of the Monster character table is a rational integer or a quadratic
irrationality.  We encode each entry uniformly as a triple `(A, B, R) : Int x Int x Int`
standing for the algebraic number `(A + B * sqrt R) / 2`.
A rational integer `m` is stored as `(2*m, 0, 0)`.  Complex conjugation of an entry
is `(A, B, R)` maps to `(A, -B, R)` when `R < 0` (an imaginary quadratic
irrationality) and the identity when `R >= 0` (a real value).
The table is stored as a string literal `charTableRaw` (rows separated by newlines,
the `194` entries of a row separated by spaces, and the three components of an entry
separated by commas) and parsed by `charTable`.  Storing the data as text keeps
elaboration cheap; all checks below are evaluated by `native_decide` on the parsed
table.
## What is machine-verified
* `charTable_nrows`, `charTable_ncols` : the table is `194 x 194`.
* `classSizes_length`, `sum_classSizes` : there are `194` conjugacy classes and the
  class sizes sum to the order of the Monster.
* `charTable_degrees` : the first column (values on the identity class) is the list
  of the `194` irreducible degrees, matching `MonsterIrreps.monsterIrrepDims`.
* `monster_characters_orthonormal` : **first orthogonality relation.**  For every
  pair of irreducible characters `chi_i, chi_k`,
  `sum_c |class c| * chi_i(c) * conj(chi_k(c)) = |M| * delta_ik`,
  the sum running over all `194` classes.  Because the entries are quadratic, the
  identity is checked by splitting each weighted sum into its rational and
  irrational components (all integer sums) and verifying the rational component
  equals `|M|*delta` while the irrational components vanish.  This single Boolean
  check, discharged by `native_decide`, ties together all `194^2 = 37636` inner
  products and certifies the whole table.
The deep inputs (that this is the character table of the Monster) are classical and
far beyond current Mathlib; the table is used as data obtained from the GAP
character-table library.  What is certified here is its exact internal consistency:
the `194` irreducible characters are orthonormal, and their degrees reproduce the
degrees recorded in `RequestProject/MonsterIrreps.lean`.
-/
